{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking","id":1449243,"title":"Does Clarity need reworking?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-22T06:46:02-07:00","id":1449243,"title":"Does Clarity need reworking?","content":"There is something that feels wrong with the Clarity rules. Firstly, having a system that closely resembles Health and yet differs substantially, especially considering the two rolls required, is odd.<br /> But what bothers me most is that the severity of the first roll does not affect the actual quantity of Clarity damage.<br /> <br /> What I mean is that even if you're being dragged by your Keeper back into Arcadia and forced to torture your own Touchstone, you can roll dozens of dice for the Clarity attack, but with low enough Wyrd ratings you have pretty good chances to not get any damage at all.<br /> All the circumstantial modifiers only determine whether the damage, IF ANY, is mild or severe. Conditions affect the damage roll, but so does having a Touchstone attached.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I have a bias coming from my experience. In the chronicle I'm running, Clarity breaking points don't happen very often, so when they do, I'd like it to be a meaningful moment with an impact, even if they have Wyrd 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> I haven't come up with a houserule (still not sure if it's needed), but I'm thinking about having a single roll, using half Wyrd (rounding down) as a &quot;weapon&quot; modifier, and only having severe damage when mild damage gets upgraded to severe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T07:50:58-07:00","id":1449248,"title":"","content":"I do agree that the current Clarity system is wonky, but the reason is probably to make the amount of damage much more manageable. There are a whole lot of modifiers to breaking points that can really add up under certain circumstances. Like, anything involving a changeling's Keeper can easily end up with +5 on top of the base dice pool. Not to mention that Clarity attacks from other sources can potentially end up with quite large dice pools, depending on the source. Keeping damage separate from that roll ensures that the damage dealt can be fine tuned by the devs, and not spiral out of control.<br /> But if that's the case, then the devs overcompensated. As you say, breaking points are rare (though other Clarity attacks might not be, as they're generally caused by NPCs) and it's way too easy to not get Clarity damage even on successful Clarity attack rolls.<br /> A changeling fresh out of character creation has a chance die on their Clarity damage rolls, which means damage is both incredibly unlikely and also limited to a single damage since you don't reroll a 10 on a chance die. In my experience it's incredibly common to have at least two Touchstones since that grants maximal protection. So the one thing that does actually increase the Clarity damage dice pool above chance die for the vast majority of Wyrd 1-2 changelings, is if they're subject to Clarity Conditions, which they gain from already suffering from enough Clarity damage to fill one of the last three boxes.<br /> (There is actually one exception: A Seeming Benefit on a Contract that causes a Clarity attack adds the successes on the attack as bonus dice on the Clarity damage roll, but that's the one thing I've found in the core book.)<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's completely underwhelming. If you do apply the successes of the Clarity attack directly, be advised that it's going to result in a dramatic increase of Clarity damage. As such you might not want to add automatic damage on top of that. If you want the Wyrd rating to still play a role in Clarity damage, I recommend adding it as bonus dice rather than as a &quot;weapon&quot; modifier.<br /> If you keep it as two separate rolls, then automatic damage is definitely something I'd recommend, but since the base dice pool for Clarity damage rolls is Wyrd, you might want to base the &quot;weapon&quot; modifier on something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T16:46:41-07:00","id":1449292,"title":"","content":"Each success on the attack roll adding a die to the damage roll is the obvious middle ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T18:00:09-07:00","id":1449498,"title":"","content":"Definitely an underwhelming system.<br /> <br /> I see what they were trying to do, but it is not well-executed. It feels like it was written by someone used to writing for OWoD with the &quot;attack roll then damage roll&quot; model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T00:14:49-07:00","id":1449516,"title":"","content":"Although staying at low Wyrd...isn't great.<br /> <br /> This does mean that you're going to take a hit on Contract rolls (and Clash of Wills if there's crossover or NPCs of the other splats), and less amount of max Glamour, which means...not being as good at doing fae-things.<br /> <br /> So unless if the game is deliberately a Tier 1 game where it might as well be a Fae-touched-only game or fae antagonists rarely ever come up and the PC motley mostly only deals with mortal antagonists,you'd be deliberately gimping yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T01:06:33-07:00","id":1449521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1449516#post1449516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although staying at low Wyrd...isn't great.<br /> <br /> This does mean that you're going to take a hit on Contract rolls (and Clash of Wills if there's crossover or NPCs of the other splats), and less amount of max Glamour, which means...not being as good at doing fae-things.<br /> <br /> So unless if the game is deliberately a Tier 1 game where it might as well be a Fae-touched-only game or fae antagonists rarely ever come up and the PC motley mostly only deals with mortal antagonists,you'd be deliberately gimping yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Define low Wyrd. As far as I've seen of others posting online, most games seems to peter out at or before [powerstat] 3, and anything above [powerstat] 5 being extremely rare. At Wyrd 3 you roll a single die (assuming two attached Touchstones), meaning you generally don't get any Clarity damage, and at Wyrd 5 you've finally reached the point where you average one damage per Clarity damage roll.<br /> And since Wits and Composure are the two most important Attributes in their respective categories (on top of changelings being further incentivised to increase both of them) there's a good chance even a medium length game won't reach the stage when you start getting Clarity Conditions.<br /> <br /> But all that aside, don't you think the Clarity system should at all matter regardless of whether it's a low tier game, a shorter game, or just the start of a longer game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T05:52:18-07:00","id":1449546,"title":"","content":"I agree about Clarity; I\u2019m not a big fan of how it currently works. In my current game, it seems as though several of the players are constantly going into comas. <br /> <br /> Before anyone asks, my Storyteller is not over-applying Clarity checks. We usually do one, maybe two, per session. It\u2019s simply that we seem to roll HORRIBLY when it comes to Clarity. Granted, the PCs have decent Wyrd ratings: one is Wyrd 5, and nearly everyone else is Wyrd 4. Average Clarity track is 5-6 boxes.<br /> <br /> In one scene, right before a major battle, our characters were presented with evidence of our experiences being unreal (a four-dice Clarity breaking point). Even though we all came in with zero Clarity damage, half of the group ended up with enough damage to immediately drop into fucking comas. It derailed the plot for several sessions, and the comatose PCs missed out on an important battle.<br /> <br /> This has been a somewhat reoccurring thing. Every few sessions, someone falls into a coma and we have to stop what we\u2019re doing to help get them out, or wait for them to wake themselves up. It\u2019s gotten to the point where we can\u2019t stand Clarity... it\u2019s just not fun anymore. AGAIN, my Storyteller is not especially harsh with Clarity rolls... we really just roll THAT badly.<br /> <br /> I dislike the Comatose Condition because I dislike mechanics that forcefully remove a player from the group and the game. Consequently, in the case of mild Clarity damage, my Storyteller now inflicts the Madness Condition in place of Comatose. MY GOD is it an improvement! It keeps the afflicted player with the group and doesn\u2019t derail active plot lines. Comatose is reserved for taking a full track of severe damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","user":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","date":". 05-25-2021, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","name":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T06:44:37-07:00","id":1449549,"title":"","content":"The odds of taking five points of clarity damage in a single roll at Wyrd 5 (through the one dot of reduction that a touchstone offers) is 0,45%. This drops to 0,09% if you have that second touchstone. At wyrd 4, the odds are 0,14% and 0,09% respectively. Assuming 'half the group' is two people, in the most likely to happen scenario (the Wyrd 5 and one of the Wyrd 4 persons took 5 clarity damage each) there's a 0,06% chance of them going from 'no clarity damage to comatose.'<br /> <br /> I always saw the comatose part as a sort of equivalent of vampires going into torpor when they have no blood left. Getting to that point shouldn't be a mild inconvenience, but I don't see a reason why it would have to derail several sessions either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T10:05:40-07:00","id":1449564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1449521#post1449521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define low Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>1-2<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But all that aside, don't you think the Clarity system should at all matter regardless of whether it's a low tier game, a shorter game, or just the start of a longer game? </div> </div> </div>TBH this isn't really an issue exclusive to CtL2e.<br /> <br /> A few of OPP's other games don't really hold up for certain modes of play and are generally written with the assumption of being a longform chronicle and don't usually account for shorter one-shot games. The expectation of players raising Wyrd high enough over time being one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T13:39:46-07:00","id":1449580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1449564#post1449564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> TBH this isn't really an issue exclusive to CtL2e.<br /> <br /> A few of OPP's other games don't really hold up for certain modes of play and are generally written with the assumption of being a longform chronicle and don't usually account for shorter one-shot games. The expectation of players raising Wyrd high enough over time being one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still going to take multiple sessions to get out of the Wyrd 1-2 period, and equally as many to reach Wyrd 5 where Clarity actually starts to properly affect the game (ignoring extreme outliers like Vintervalpen's example). After four sessions I've earned 6 XP and 2 Beats (after subtracting extra starting XP and extra beats gained per session, which we usually do to bump up XP gain rates), meaning that after four sessions I could buy a single Wyrd increase if I don't buy any Skills, Attributes, Contracts or Merits that aren't just a single dot.<br /> If that's the average rate of XP gain for others as well (I don't know, but I don't have any other numbers so it's what I'll run with) then it'll take 13 sessions of play before you can reach Wyrd 5 provided you don't spend any XP on anything else (or 10 sessions if you spent 5 of your starting Merit dots on Wyrd 2).<br /> <br /> I do agree that CofD games (don't know enough about their other franchises) are at their best when played in longer campaigns, but surely you don't expect a campaign to reach a double digit amount of session before a core system in the game actually comes into play? Compare with Integrity, Humanity, Wisdom, and Harmony where it matters from the very first session. And it's a good thing that they do, because they inform some very important themes in those games. It's just weird that Changeling, a game with very clear themes that even has it as a type of Health track (which implies increased mobility), practically ignores that part from the start, only pushing it into the game in small increments after the players already have played for some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T20:39:18-07:00","id":1449612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1449580#post1449580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just weird that Changeling, a game with very clear themes that even has it as a type of Health track (which implies increased mobility), practically ignores that part from the start, only pushing it into the game in small increments after the players already have played for some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarity as a Health track implies increased <i>granularity</i> along with the less unique quality of not requiring experience to recover it. Satiety is flatly the most wildly variable Integrity analogue of the bunch (you can literally gain or lose eight points in a single stroke), but Beasts don't need to track whether bouncing back is easier or harder except at the very ends of the scale, which it accomplishes through Satiety constantly applying one Condition or another to the character.<br /> <br /> A changeling character with average stats starts with a maximum Clarity of 4-6. Clarity is also an Integrity model that only provides Beats when it's damaged and it's imperiled by common Conditions and basic social situations like rejection, lies, and broken promises as experienced by a character that literally can yank people's emotions in a direction at any time. The fact that most Clarity damage rolls you make will be little more than a tense roll to see if you flip your perception bonus to a penalty is roughly equivalent to Vampire's starting characters having next to nothing to worry about from short exposure to sunlight \u2014 it's there to get rougher as the game progresses further into the supernatural end of things.<br /> <br /> The pressures of Huntsmen and the benefits of magic and the Beat incentives for being inconvenienced by oaths and tokens are the game's tools for pushing the characters further into the supernatural end of things. &quot;If you build a perceptive character and play them in a risk-averse fashion while the world doesn't make staying clear-headed less than your top priority, Clarity doesn't do much&quot; is a non-statement \u2014 you can literally say the same thing about Cover or Harmony, replacing &quot;perceptive&quot; and &quot;clear-headed with words reflective of their respective Traits.<br /> <br /> Make no mistake, the mortal world is arguably the most preferable one for a changeling to rebuild her life in, but keeping up social interactions prior to building that space out is going to involve pretty frequent minor tests of your ability to trust your sense of reality, because the Chronicles of Darkness are a setting where people routinely say &quot;that didn't happen,&quot; &quot;yeah, sure, I'll do that,&quot; &quot;I never want to see you again,&quot; and so on in relation to weird strangers who know too much about their loved ones and don't seem to know what day of the week it is (or are fixated on definitely knowing what day of the week it is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-25-2021, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T00:25:03-07:00","id":1449623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1449612#post1449612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that most Clarity damage rolls you make will be little more than a tense roll to see if you flip your perception bonus to a penalty[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Provided the Clarity attack roll succeeds. It's a two step process, making the already low chance of taking Clarity damage even lower.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The pressures of Huntsmen and the benefits of magic and the Beat incentives for being inconvenienced by oaths and tokens are the game's tools for pushing the characters further into the supernatural end of things. &quot;If you build a perceptive character and play them in a risk-averse fashion while the world doesn't make staying clear-headed less than your top priority, Clarity doesn't do much&quot; is a non-statement \u2014 you can literally say the same thing about Cover or Harmony, replacing &quot;perceptive&quot; and &quot;clear-headed with words reflective of their respective Traits. </div> </div> </div>In a way, my experience has been the exact opposite. Looking at the example breaking point list, it seems to me that humans would be much more likely to cause a breaking point, if only due to their ignorance. Otherwise it's mostly stuff even a daredevil (literally my character's Needle) would try to avoid, such as killings, torture, and direct contact with True Fae/Arcadia.<br /> After four sessions of play (which mostly consists of Hedge delving, and discussing supernatural matters with other Changelings, interspersed with a dream journey and being hunted by an unknown supernatural being, so definitely in the supernatural end of things) I've taken a single breaking point (3 dice, Clarity attack roll failed so I didn't get to roll a single die for Clarity damage), and that's only because extra starting XP allowed me to reach Wyrd 3 quite early. I would've taken a second breaking point for reaping Glamour if not for the Pure Clarity Contract, but on the other hand I wouldn't have reaped Glamour if I didn't have that Contract in the first place since I had no pressure while filling up the Glamour reserves.<br /> Right now, the big breaking point generator would be if my ST started putting out antagonists with mind affecting powers, but barring that I'd say that the supernatural end of things, while having larger Clarity damage roll dice pools (if we assume games generally become more supernaturally loaded further into a campaign), still largely fails to engage with the Clarity system.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;If you build a perceptive character and play them in a risk-averse fashion while the world doesn't make staying clear-headed less than your top priority, Clarity doesn't do much&quot; is a non-statement </div> </div> </div>A non-statement not stated anywhere. In all the other games I've played (CofD, VtR, MtA, WtF, DtR), only Werewolf has an Integrity equivalent that you can end up accidentally not engaging with since acting as a werewolf makes your Harmony stationary (a problem I've discussed elsewhere). In CofD and Deviant it's literally impossible to not engage with Integrity or Loyalty/Conviction because the core gameplay revolves around those traits. In Vampire and Mage you're always pushed towards behaviour which is counter to Humanity and Wisdom in a way that only risk averse gameplay can avoid it. (Much more so in Vampire than in Mage, imo, but there's plenty of Understanding AoHs that can occur.)<br /> Changeling's problem is similar to Werewolf in this regard: Just playing the game doesn't necessarily lead to any breaking points at all. Playing risk-averse is not needed to end up with a minimal amount of breaking points. Breaking points that arise from the character's behaviour requires quite frankly drastic behaviour, and breaking points that are inflicted on the character by others or by circumstances are highly dependent on the ST facilitating them. (Barring a few unique breaking points such as meeting your Fetch for the first time or reaching various Wyrd thresholds.) It's a shame because in Vampire no one needs to make a conscious effort to engage with Humanity because that happens naturally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-26-2021, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T11:07:21-07:00","id":1449673,"title":"","content":"In my current Chronicle, my players are freshly escaped from Arcadia. They were specifically targeted because they'd all made strong oaths together even before being abducted (circumstances made wyrd take note, I won't get into it now) and all broke those oaths.<br /> <br /> So I've started all my players with Hunted (Persistent), Oathbreaker (Persistent) and no attached Touchstones (though they can still get their first for free once they make a connection to someone). This increases their damage from 1 dice, to 5 (+1 for each of the conditions, +2 for no attached touchstone).<br /> They're all finding out what happened to their old lives, meeting their fetches for the first time, and so on.<br /> <br /> One of my player even has a maximum Clarity of 3...<br /> <br /> So, with there being multiple clarity attacks per scene (some very high attack dice pools) because of them constantly discovering bad stuff about what happened in their absence and being rejected by loved ones or meeting fetches for the first time, all damage being 5 dice minimum, and them not having any attached Touchstones to heal Clarity damage with, you'd expect them to all go rushing to secure Touchstones to get out of this inevitable downward spiral, right?<br /> <br /> Eh, not really. There's been a few Clarity Conditions but nothing bad and nobody feels too much in danger. And that's with all of the above circumstances after 20 or so hours of play. xD<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's a bit too easy. Another ten hours of play and my players will start dropping if they don't secure Touchstones and fix their persistent conditions. But look how long they're lasting with 5x the normal damage for their Wyrd level, and no Touchstones. :P<br /> <br /> I like the idea behind the system though, it just needs more bite at the low end. I'd probably increase the base attack pool (To let's say, 3 dice at Wyrd 1. Or add successes on attack to the damage dice pool, why not? Though then again, that would make all exceptional successes also big hits), make Touchstone interactions only make you roll Wits + Composure and heal that many clarity boxes of mild or 1 box of severe damage, and make having attached Touchstones not reduce your clarity damage pool by so much.<br /> And maybe make being full on clarity damage not instantly put you in coma then, but make Resolve + Composure rolls to stave it off every hour or every ten minutes or something. Like full bashing damage and trying to stay conscious out, but for your Clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 05-26-2021, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T17:22:39-07:00","id":1450102,"title":"","content":"By comparing Unahim's and Tessie's experience (which of course do not constitute a statistical basis), I get the feeling that the authors made some assumptions about the kind of stories that would be played in Changeling.<br /> If you focus the story on retaking or rebuilding your personal connections and emotional investments then breaking points should come up more often and with higher modifiers (but even then, damage may be rare).<br /> But if you're mostly dealing with supernatural matters, you won't engage with Clarity as much. <br /> My own experience running Changeling is pretty similar to Tessie's: mostly supernatural mystery-driven, since my players don't seem to really care about their past lives, their Fetches etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1449612#post1449612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity as a Health track implies increased <i>granularity</i> along with the less unique quality of not requiring experience to recover it. Satiety is flatly the most wildly variable Integrity analogue of the bunch (you can literally gain or lose eight points in a single stroke), but Beasts don't need to track whether bouncing back is easier or harder except at the very ends of the scale, which it accomplishes through Satiety constantly applying one Condition or another to the character.<br /> <br /> A changeling character with average stats starts with a maximum Clarity of 4-6. Clarity is also an Integrity model that only provides Beats when it's damaged and it's imperiled by common Conditions and basic social situations like rejection, lies, and broken promises as experienced by a character that literally can yank people's emotions in a direction at any time. The fact that most Clarity damage rolls you make will be little more than a tense roll to see if you flip your perception bonus to a penalty is roughly equivalent to Vampire's starting characters having next to nothing to worry about from short exposure to sunlight \u2014 it's there to get rougher as the game progresses further into the supernatural end of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it is meant to have more granularity, but in practice it achieves the opposite.<br /> Other Integrity traits range from 1 to 10, starting from 7, and cause a dot loss with a single Breaking Point failure.<br /> Compare it with an average Clarity track of 4-6, which gives less room for smaller effects, not more. <br /> The result is an all-or-nothing effect, where either you get no damage, or, with high enough Wyrd, get straight to Comatose with a single attack (considering Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot's case)<br /> <br /> Clarity should be more like an ordinary Integrity trait, but instead of losing one dot, you get a bunch of damage. You heal some over time, then you get some more etc.<br /> That is fluid and granular, like Health, with enough room to range from lightly affected to full madness or comatose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1449673#post1449673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea behind the system though, it just needs more bite at the low end. I'd probably increase the base attack pool (To let's say, 3 dice at Wyrd 1. Or add successes on attack to the damage dice pool, why not? Though then again, that would make all exceptional successes also big hits), make Touchstone interactions only make you roll Wits + Composure and heal that many clarity boxes of mild or 1 box of severe damage, and make having attached Touchstones not reduce your clarity damage pool by so much.<br /> And maybe make being full on clarity damage not instantly put you in coma then, but make Resolve + Composure rolls to stave it off every hour or every ten minutes or something. Like full bashing damage and trying to stay conscious out, but for your Clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, there shouldn't be a Comatose condition when filled with mild damage, at the very least rolling to stave it off seems a good solution.<br /> Also:<br /> - severe damage should only happen as an upgrade of mild damage, not from a severe attack (or at least it should only be allowed in extremely rare cases<br /> - successful attacks should make at least 1 damage (similarly to how breaking point failures automatically cause a dot loss)<br /> - there should be more and easier ways to heal single mild damages, perhaps automatically healing a bit over time<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if it would be better to have a fixed Clarity range of 1-10...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T19:36:31-07:00","id":1450256,"title":"","content":"Of all the content from the first draft of Second Edition that did not make it into the final product I miss the draft rules for Clarity the most. Specifically I thought that it was a brilliant design choice to have success on a breaking point roll give you a chance to increase your Clarity level. It incentivized confronting your trauma under controlled circumstances, pushing yourself to step out of your safe zone a little at a time in a way that felt very true to my own experiences with trauma and the healing thereof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T10:16:57-07:00","id":1450465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1450256#post1450256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of all the content from the first draft of Second Edition that did not make it into the final product I miss the draft rules for Clarity the most. Specifically I thought that it was a brilliant design choice to have success on a breaking point roll give you a chance to increase your Clarity level. It incentivized confronting your trauma under controlled circumstances, pushing yourself to step out of your safe zone a little at a time in a way that felt very true to my own experiences with trauma and the healing thereof.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is there any place those of us who didn't back the Kickstarter could get a view of those rules? I'd be very curious to see!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T17:19:31-07:00","id":1450521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1450465#post1450465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any place those of us who didn't back the Kickstarter could get a view of those rules? I'd be very curious to see!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9HTbTc08O4ISWpIbnU4dmlGY2c/view\" target=\"_blank\">Page 64-9.</a> My experience running a game with them (where one character had a Wits + Composure pool of 9 and another had a pool of 3) has not painted a picture of their being less all-or-nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T13:15:18-07:00","id":1452525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1450102#post1450102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it is meant to have more granularity, but in practice it achieves the opposite.<br /> Other Integrity traits range from 1 to 10, starting from 7, and cause a dot loss with a single Breaking Point failure.<br /> Compare it with an average Clarity track of 4-6, which gives less room for smaller effects, not more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that Icons increase the Clarity track too, so more granularity can be achieved. And characters will increase attributes over time, and certainly can start above 4-6, especially with +1 from Seeming Favored Attribute. I can make very feasible character builds that start with 7-8 Clarity without being weird.<br /> On top of that, I've never played a Vampire game where anyone had more than 7 Humanity at any point, or a Mage game with more than 7 Wisdom, so the 8-10 range is very, very theoretical to me...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree, there shouldn't be a Comatose condition when filled with mild damage, at the very least rolling to stave it off seems a good solution.<br /> Also:<br /> - severe damage should only happen as an upgrade of mild damage, not from a severe attack (or at least it should only be allowed in extremely rare cases<br /> - successful attacks should make at least 1 damage (similarly to how breaking point failures automatically cause a dot loss)<br /> - there should be more and easier ways to heal single mild damages, perhaps automatically healing a bit over time<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if it would be better to have a fixed Clarity range of 1-10... </div> </div> </div>Here are the house rules I'll be trying out:<br /> - Successful clarity attacks always deal at least 1 Clarity damage to the Changeling. Successes on the damage roll add to this damage.<br /> - An exceptional success on a clarity attack does not cause the attack to do severe clarity damage. Instead it might inflict a Tilt, such as Insensate, or cause the Changeling to Incite Bedlam involuntarily. Or other things like that. (On that note, during Involuntary Bedlam, I always count them as rolling 3 successes to eliminate differences between characters, and I don't let players choose to do this, as I found they were too &quot;easy beats&quot; for too much disruption in play.)<br /> - Characters only gain a Beat for clarity damage in the 3 last boxes.<br /> - If all boxes are full with mild clarity damage, the character does not gain Comatose. They gain a different Clarity condition as normal. The character is mentally unstable, and must roll Wits + Composure every scene or suffer 1 Clarity damage. As soon as they heal or downgrade any amount of Clarity damage, they stabilize for the moment (even if they're still full on mild damage) until they take more Clarity damage again, so long as they're full on mild after that damage of course.<br /> - When all boxes are full with mild damage, additional damage rolls over into Severe damage.<br /> - If all boxes are full with Severe damage, the Changeling gains the Comatose (Persistent) Condition, and will likely die if they don't get help.<br /> - Meaningful interaction with a Touchstone (attached or not) during a Chapter lets you roll Wits + Composure + (number of attached Touchstones). You may downgrade a number of Clarity damage equal to 1 + successes rolled. You first downgrade any severe damage to mild, and then any mild damage to fully healed.<br /> - Touchstones no longer reduce the dice in the damage rolls.<br /> - When you regain 1 Willpower from your Thread, you may downgrade 1 Clarity damage, starting with Severe.<br /> - When you regain all Willpower from your Thread, you may do the same roll as if you interacted with a Touchstone, and downgrade that much Clarity damage.<br /> - Healing from Clarity conditions stays the same.<br /> <br /> I think that should do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 06-16-2021, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T08:00:53-07:00","id":1453276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1450521#post1450521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9HTbTc08O4ISWpIbnU4dmlGY2c/view\" target=\"_blank\">Page 64-9.</a> My experience running a game with them (where one character had a Wits + Composure pool of 9 and another had a pool of 3) has not painted a picture of their being less all-or-nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, this was a godsend.<br /> <br /> These Clarity rules work similarly to Integrity, where the Changeling can tailor his owns Breaking Points, but they have to follow a ruleset of conditions. This works so much better for my table because I am getting to the point where powerfull changelings (Wyrd 5+) are being confronted with their Durances trying to recover some other Losts that have been captured, and things are going Comatose way too much.<br /> <br /> IMHO those Breaking Points occurs way too much or inviabilize some minor things(parentesis for explanation):<br /> <br /> 1-die<br /> - Going one full day without human or changeling contact. (No &quot;witch of the woods&quot; steryotype for powerful changelings)<br /> - Breaking a mundane promise.<br /> <br /> 2-dice<br /> - Eating nothing but goblin fruit for a full day.<br /> - Having someone break a mundane promise to you.<br /> - Discover that someone lied to you about something minor.<br /> - Gaining a non-Clarity Condition that confuses your senses or badly jars you, such as Lost or Spooked.<br /> <br /> 3-dice<br /> - Killing someone else\u2019s fetch.<br /> - Reaching Wyrd 3.<br /> - Having a mortal shun or disparage you.<br /> <br /> 4-dice<br /> - Discovering that someone lied to you about something important.<br /> - Death of a family member. (This should not push you towards fae nature, but human nature)<br /> <br /> The way those breaking points are presented, they should be more stronger for lower Wyrd Changelings. As it is, powerful changelings can't do much without going to sleep(Comatose) for minor and random events. And they inviabilise characters that try to overcome their problems and accept that the past cannot be changed and try to move on with their lifes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 06-23-2021, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T11:08:28-07:00","id":1453659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1453276#post1453276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[SNIP]</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really follow here.<br /> <br /> It isn't non-viable to move on with your life. You simply make new friends and get contact with new changelings. Nothing in that list says you need to fix your old life, at all.<br /> <br /> Messing with situations close to your own Durance <i>should</i> be hard, that is a core theme of the game. The &quot;witch of the wood&quot; archetype is pretty clearly more of a True Fae archetype (it would be an <i>excellent</i> Title), balancing Clarity is about balancing both sides of your true nature, &quot;witch of the wood&quot; essentially rejects all links to the things that keep you grounded in Ironsides, not just Arcadia.<br /> Remember that Changelings aren't just &quot;people with cool fae magical abilities&quot;, they walk on the knife edge of sanity, balancing their attachments to both worlds.<br /> <br /> &quot;Death of a family member.&quot; is in there because Changelings can become 4 times as old as humans, and also because it can be a shock to discover what happened in your absence, I guess. Remember you can always use your own judgement on these.<br /> <br /> I'm having trouble seeing how your players go Comatose so fast. Wyrd 5+ Changelings would surely have recovered a few Icons, and should have enough experience that if they had weak Wits + Composure to begin with, they could have shored that up by now. So I'm assuming 7-8 Clarity would be about the lowest in the party here.<br /> <br /> They could easily have at least 2 Touchstones each, but certainly have 1 each. Let's also use 3-dice Clarity attacks as a baseline since it's smack in the middle.<br /> <br /> 3 dice for attacks means 34% of attacks fail straight off the bat. The remaining 66% then trigger a 3 dice or 4 dice clarity damage roll (depending on touchstones)<br /> 1 touchstone = 4 damage dice = average of 1.33 damage<br /> 2 touchstone = 3 damage dice = average of 1 damage<br /> <br /> That means an attack on average deals 0.88 if they have 1 touchstones, and 0.66 damage if they have 2+ touchstones. In other words, they should be able to make it through 7-8 clarity attacks without falling unconscious, on average.<br /> If they're taking more attacks than that it's probably common sense that they'd start dropping, they're putting themselves under strain they're not supposed to.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind they get clarity conditions for the last 3 boxes, and resolving those instantly heals some clarity, and most are easy to resolve.<br /> <br /> If they get more overwhelmed, zipping back to Ironsides for a bit to recover is sensible.<br /> <br /> Your easiest house rule would be to not use Comatose for mild damage, but let mild damage roll over into serious damage and only inflict Comatose once they're full on serious damage. That way they'll take close to 20 clarity attacks on average to get to Comatose, plenty of advance warning before they need R&amp;R; and the amount of rolls mitigates the chance of bad luck somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 06-27-2021, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T14:24:31-07:00","id":1453666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1453659#post1453659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your easiest house rule would be to not use Comatose for mild damage, but let mild damage roll over into serious damage and only inflict Comatose once they're full on serious damage. That way they'll take close to 20 clarity attacks on average to get to Comatose, plenty of advance warning before they need R&amp;R; and the amount of rolls mitigates the chance of bad luck somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only one that has 2 Touchstones, got their second one because of a Entitlement.<br /> <br /> This helps with some of the problems.<br /> <br /> They are getting Comatose because they are dealing with some frequency with those 3 situations:<br /> <br /> 2-dice<br /> - Having someone break a mundane promise to you.<br /> - Discover that someone lied to you about something minor.<br /> <br /> 4-dice<br /> - Discovering that someone lied to you about something important.<br /> <br /> Part of that its because they are trying to use clever wordplay to get something good from bargains and promises, but most normal people don't tend to remember specific details about little promises. Also, they are dealing with secret societies, that tend to lie a lot to cover their secrets. And I already said that they should just try to make simplier bargains. But my table was looking for a &quot;I'm a half/fae with powers, fleeing from some eldritch horror, I'm going to go loud if needed&quot;. and not &quot;Please don't lie to me, it hurts my feelings and I can't cope very well with this&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T19:30:16-07:00","id":1453677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1453659#post1453659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your easiest house rule would be to not use Comatose for mild damage, but let mild damage roll over into serious damage and only inflict Comatose once they're full on serious damage. That way they'll take close to 20 clarity attacks on average to get to Comatose, plenty of advance warning before they need R&amp;R; and the amount of rolls mitigates the chance of bad luck somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternately, pick up a wild entitlement, which changes out the Comatose Condition for the Cockaigne Condition and provides a much more &quot;go loud&quot; balancing act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T09:26:22-07:00","id":1453697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449243-does-clarity-need-reworking?p=1453666#post1453666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of that its because they are trying to use clever wordplay to get something good from bargains and promises, but most normal people don't tend to remember specific details about little promises. Also, they are dealing with secret societies, that tend to lie a lot to cover their secrets. And I already said that they should just try to make simplier bargains. But my table was looking for a &quot;I'm a half/fae with powers, fleeing from some eldritch horror, I'm going to go loud if needed&quot;. and not &quot;Please don't lie to me, it hurts my feelings and I can't cope very well with this&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't they simply spend some time with their Touchstones here and there? It heals <i>all</i> mild Clarity damage right away after some meaningful interaction.<br /> <br /> Clarity is not about &quot;hurting your feelings&quot;, it's about shaking the foundations on which the character is trying to reconstruct a stable view of reality. Remember that the tagline of the game is &quot;beautiful <i>madness</i>&quot;; Changelings have trouble with slipping sanity. When they find out they've been lied to, it calls into question everything they think is real, and the problem is they can't remember very well what is and isn't real because they left so much of themselves on the Thorns.<br /> Even the death of the family member is not about emotions, it's about a stable part of your life up to that point suddenly being gone. We identify by our family members to some extent.<br /> <br /> If you're using &quot;this does/doesn't hurt my feelings&quot; as the baseline for what should and shouldn't cause Clarity damage, you might be portraying it in a way that is counter to what it is actually meant to be. Which is your prerogative of course, but it might be part of the reason why you feel you need individual breaking points that differ between characters.<br /> <br /> Note that the &quot;eldritch horrors&quot; they're fleeing from are also not good at outright lying, relying more on wordplay, since they're bound up in these rules even tighter than the Changelings themselves are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}